Subject: [PATCH] projectm-eval: per-thread state for rand()

The Mersenne Twister state behind the expression language's rand() was a
process-wide static. ProjectM TV runs a second projectM instance on a background
thread (it compiles the next preset's shaders, which also runs the preset's init
code), so two threads could use the state at once: one could pass the refill
check while the other advanced the index, and then read one element past the
array. With per-thread state each thread gets the same sequence as before (same
fixed seed).

---
diff --git a/vendor/projectm-eval/projectm-eval/TreeFunctions.c b/vendor/projectm-eval/projectm-eval/TreeFunctions.c
index cf1a2c0..f60e060 100644
--- a/vendor/projectm-eval/projectm-eval/TreeFunctions.c
+++ b/vendor/projectm-eval/projectm-eval/TreeFunctions.c
@@ -169,8 +169,9 @@ static uint32_t prjm_eval_genrand_int32(void)
     static uint32_t mag01[2] = { 0x0UL, MATRIX_A };
     /* mag01[x] = x * MATRIX_A  for x=0,1 */
 
-    static uint32_t mt[N]; /* the array for the state vector  */
-    static int32_t mti; /* mti==N+1 means mt[N] is not initialized */
+    /* Per thread: several projectM instances may evaluate code on different threads at once. */
+    static _Thread_local uint32_t mt[N]; /* the array for the state vector  */
+    static _Thread_local int32_t mti; /* mti==N+1 means mt[N] is not initialized */
 
 
     if (!mti)
